# This repo is cloned onto an Ubuntu GPU box. Everything checks out LF.
#
# core.autocrlf is true on the Windows machine that authors it, so without this
# a checkout writes CRLF into the working copy, and the runbook scp's that copy
# straight to Linux -- where bash answers a CRLF script with "\r: command not
# found", which reads as a missing interpreter rather than a line-ending bug.
# workshop/_strip-crlf.sh exists because this already happened once.
#
# text=auto still leaves detected binaries (png, pdf, woff2) untouched.
* text=auto eol=lf
